  "diagnosis": "The test sent an invalid greeting and immediately dropped its peer before the server greeting/validation. Windows can report a connection reset before InvalidData, which production correctly treats as ordinary peer teardown. The fixture therefore could not reliably require a bad-peer failure count. The correction retains and reads the test connection through validation; production transport and numerical behavior do not change.",
